WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.284
- I'm Mike and I think
ghosts are bull (beep).

00:00:02.284 --> 00:00:05.123
(relaxed music)

00:00:06.693 --> 00:00:07.631
- What would the ghosts look like?

00:00:07.631 --> 00:00:09.767
I saw Ghostbusters, like Slimer?

00:00:09.767 --> 00:00:11.789
- Sometimes, people lose loved ones.

00:00:11.789 --> 00:00:13.297
They're attached to the idea that

00:00:13.297 --> 00:00:14.923
they could find their loved ones

00:00:14.923 --> 00:00:16.113
in the paranormal form.

00:00:16.113 --> 00:00:17.662
- In the entire course of

00:00:17.662 --> 00:00:19.631
people owning cameras,

00:00:19.631 --> 00:00:21.117
we don't have one piece of evidence

00:00:21.117 --> 00:00:22.114
that ghosts exist.

00:00:22.114 --> 00:00:23.976
- If I'm scared, it's
because I'm in the dark

00:00:23.976 --> 00:00:25.417
in the middle of nowhere.

00:00:25.417 --> 00:00:26.875
- The only thing I'm afraid of at night

00:00:26.875 --> 00:00:28.623
is a criminal coming up to me

00:00:28.623 --> 00:00:29.893
and stabbing me in the throat.

00:00:29.893 --> 00:00:32.038
- I'm nervous, my heart is
palpitating a little bit.

00:00:32.038 --> 00:00:34.907
- I heard that ghosts get
angry when they see red.

00:00:34.907 --> 00:00:36.738
So, I'm human bait.

00:00:36.738 --> 00:00:37.672
Come at me, ghosts.

00:00:37.672 --> 00:00:39.635
- It's gonna be fun.

00:00:39.635 --> 00:00:40.594
(sigh)

00:00:40.594 --> 00:00:44.370
(suspenseful music)

00:00:45.820 --> 00:00:47.823
- I have a Ghostbusters pillowcase at home

00:00:47.823 --> 00:00:49.765
that I believe is real.

00:00:49.765 --> 00:00:51.762
But ghosts are not real.

00:01:00.716 --> 00:01:04.128
We're here at the
supposed abandoned asylum.

00:01:04.128 --> 00:01:05.723
We're about to go inside.

00:01:05.723 --> 00:01:08.785
(ominous music)

00:01:08.785 --> 00:01:09.829
- My name is Chad.

00:01:09.829 --> 00:01:12.044
I'm co-founder of Amendella Paranormal.

00:01:12.044 --> 00:01:13.467
- I'm Josh, I'm the founder.

00:01:13.467 --> 00:01:16.027
- This is an asylum
that I had found before.

00:01:16.027 --> 00:01:18.885
It's been kinda locally known.

00:01:18.885 --> 00:01:21.842
- There's no actual address to this place.

00:01:21.842 --> 00:01:23.235
No real roads here.

00:01:23.235 --> 00:01:24.840
- [Chad] Literally in
the middle of nowhere.

00:01:24.840 --> 00:01:27.515
- There's no actual evidence
of this being an asylum.

00:01:27.515 --> 00:01:29.120
It's all folklore.

00:01:29.120 --> 00:01:30.108
- How you feeling, Jason?

00:01:30.108 --> 00:01:31.285
- I'm feeling great.

00:01:31.285 --> 00:01:33.093
I'm actually more
interested in the graffiti.

00:01:33.093 --> 00:01:35.666
- We're going to be going in through here.

00:01:35.666 --> 00:01:36.864
Everybody be careful.

00:01:36.864 --> 00:01:37.891
- A couple things that we've gotten here,

00:01:37.891 --> 00:01:39.547
we've gotten a lot of voices.

00:01:39.547 --> 00:01:42.505
Me and Daniel actually
heard a little boy laughing.

00:01:42.505 --> 00:01:43.654
- We've gotten EMF hits here,

00:01:43.654 --> 00:01:45.706
confirming that there is some spirit

00:01:45.706 --> 00:01:48.244
that either believes they're
a nurse or was once a nurse.

00:01:48.244 --> 00:01:49.049
You will probably find that you'll

00:01:49.049 --> 00:01:50.381
wanna stay closer to the walls.

00:01:50.381 --> 00:01:51.752
Most people feel better in the dark

00:01:51.752 --> 00:01:54.284
when they have something behind them.

00:01:54.284 --> 00:01:56.144
- Just keep your mind
open, keep your ears open.

00:01:56.144 --> 00:01:58.074
Sometimes you'll feel like a slight touch,

00:01:58.074 --> 00:02:01.121
a breath, or, it's real
subtle, you know what I mean?

00:02:01.121 --> 00:02:02.881
- Is it just me, or does
everyone now feel like

00:02:02.881 --> 00:02:04.406
they're feeling breaths and touches?

00:02:04.406 --> 00:02:05.189
(laughter)

00:02:05.189 --> 00:02:06.269
(mechanical beeping)

00:02:06.269 --> 00:02:06.829
- [Voiceover] So.

00:02:06.829 --> 00:02:07.424
- [Voiceover] Yeah, so it's on now.

00:02:07.424 --> 00:02:08.379
(faint whistling sound)

00:02:08.379 --> 00:02:08.941
- [Voiceover] Right.

00:02:08.941 --> 00:02:10.716
- [Voiceover] Someone
trying to whistle, or?

00:02:10.716 --> 00:02:12.538
- [Voiceover] Definitely heard that.

00:02:12.538 --> 00:02:12.997
- [Voiceover] What was it?

00:02:12.997 --> 00:02:13.901
Yeah, so it's on now.

00:02:13.901 --> 00:02:15.625
(whistling sound)

00:02:15.625 --> 00:02:16.483
Yeah, so it's on now.

00:02:16.483 --> 00:02:17.345
(whistling sound)

00:02:17.345 --> 00:02:18.344
- [Voiceover] You heard
it, though, the whistling?

00:02:18.344 --> 00:02:19.274
- [Voiceover] I heard
it, oh yeah, for sure.

00:02:19.274 --> 00:02:20.048
- [Voiceover] What was it?

00:02:20.048 --> 00:02:20.398
- [Voiceover] I thought it was like,

00:02:20.398 --> 00:02:21.628
a cell phone or something.

00:02:21.628 --> 00:02:23.886
- [Voiceover] I don't know.

00:02:23.886 --> 00:02:25.329
- [Voiceover] Yeah, so it's on now.

00:02:25.329 --> 00:02:26.227
- [Voiceover] Right.

00:02:26.227 --> 00:02:28.104
(dramatic bangs)

00:02:28.104 --> 00:02:29.693
- [Voiceover] So we know the nurses here,

00:02:29.693 --> 00:02:30.871
do you get lonely here by yourself,

00:02:30.871 --> 00:02:32.167
or are you by yourself?

00:02:32.167 --> 00:02:33.321
- [Voiceover] What was that?

00:02:33.321 --> 00:02:34.010
- [Voiceover] The moan or whatever?

00:02:34.010 --> 00:02:34.965
- I thought I heard a moan.

00:02:34.965 --> 00:02:36.136
- [Voiceover] Yeah, it--

00:02:36.136 --> 00:02:37.262
- I heard something, there was just like

00:02:37.262 --> 00:02:38.259
a big atmospheric boom.

00:02:38.259 --> 00:02:39.104
- [Voiceover] Right here, right?

00:02:39.104 --> 00:02:39.643
- Yeah.

00:02:39.643 --> 00:02:40.622
- [Voiceover] We brought a lot of people

00:02:40.622 --> 00:02:42.421
that are very anxious to meet you.

00:02:42.421 --> 00:02:43.306
- [Voiceover] We're here
to make them believers.

00:02:43.306 --> 00:02:45.146
Are you gonna help us with that?

00:02:45.146 --> 00:02:45.949
Can you finish this for me?

00:02:45.949 --> 00:02:48.478
(slaps)

00:02:50.748 --> 00:02:52.732
(dramatic bangs)

00:02:52.732 --> 00:02:54.406
- [Voiceover] What if
you use the spirit box?

00:02:54.406 --> 00:02:56.195
- Well, we got that one.

00:02:56.195 --> 00:02:57.555
I think I hear something.

00:03:14.540 --> 00:03:16.029
- Speak louder, please.

00:03:17.285 --> 00:03:19.053
Damn, we're really not
getting anything right now.

00:03:19.053 --> 00:03:20.443
(dramatic bangs)

00:03:21.383 --> 00:03:22.444
- [Voiceover] I could see
this being fun to hang out at

00:03:22.444 --> 00:03:23.789
during the day.

00:03:23.789 --> 00:03:25.608
- [Voiceover] All right,
everybody let's get in a circle.

00:03:25.608 --> 00:03:27.213
Hi, you can use our energy.

00:03:27.213 --> 00:03:29.025
Can you come over here and grab one of us?

00:03:29.025 --> 00:03:30.073
Did nobody feel anything yet?

00:03:30.073 --> 00:03:31.861
- My wrist got a little itchy.

00:03:31.861 --> 00:03:32.829
- [Voiceover] Want me to get that for you?

00:03:32.829 --> 00:03:33.926
(laughter)

00:03:33.926 --> 00:03:36.324
- [Voiceover] Can you make
it colder in the circle?

00:03:36.324 --> 00:03:38.234
- [Voiceover] 73.8.

00:03:38.234 --> 00:03:39.454
(beeping)

00:03:39.454 --> 00:03:41.302
Okay, now's it's 73 even.

00:03:41.302 --> 00:03:42.948
72.3.

00:03:42.948 --> 00:03:44.078
- [Voiceover] Keep going, keep going.

00:03:44.078 --> 00:03:45.248
- [Voiceover] So it's a
four degree difference?

00:03:45.248 --> 00:03:47.361
- Yeah. 71.6.

00:03:47.361 --> 00:03:48.498
70.9.

00:03:48.498 --> 00:03:49.332
- [Voiceover] 69.

00:03:49.332 --> 00:03:50.299
- [Voiceover] It dropped seven degrees.

00:03:50.299 --> 00:03:50.867
- [Voiceover] Yeah.

00:03:50.867 --> 00:03:52.187
- [Voiceover] In the middle
of a circle of people--

00:03:52.187 --> 00:03:53.095
- [Voiceover] It should get hotter.

00:03:53.095 --> 00:03:53.967
- [Voiceover] It should never be colder,

00:03:53.967 --> 00:03:54.726
it should be warmer.

00:03:54.726 --> 00:03:56.121
- [Voiceover] Can we
do 95 degrees, please?

00:03:56.121 --> 00:03:57.970
(laughter)

00:03:57.970 --> 00:03:59.615
(dramatic bangs)

00:03:59.615 --> 00:04:02.450
(dramatic piano music)

00:04:02.450 --> 00:04:04.218
- I didn't personally see anything

00:04:04.218 --> 00:04:05.437
or experience anything.

00:04:05.437 --> 00:04:07.145
- It was just like a teen hangout spot.

00:04:07.145 --> 00:04:09.034
I wouldn't have been
surprised if we walked in

00:04:09.034 --> 00:04:10.419
on two teenagers making out.

00:04:10.419 --> 00:04:12.023
- And when you look up
and you see the stars

00:04:12.023 --> 00:04:13.914
and the stars are
actually pretty beautiful.

00:04:13.914 --> 00:04:16.026
This is really awesome,
I should go camping here.

00:04:16.026 --> 00:04:18.455
- I was creeped out by
imagining the past of the place.

00:04:18.455 --> 00:04:19.593
I was creeped out by imagining what

00:04:19.593 --> 00:04:20.621
might have gone on there.

00:04:20.621 --> 00:04:21.738
- Paranormal or not,

00:04:21.738 --> 00:04:23.405
there's just something
off-putting about that.

00:04:23.405 --> 00:04:24.827
- I dug their enthusiasm.

00:04:24.827 --> 00:04:26.799
I thought it was cool
they were so into this.

00:04:26.799 --> 00:04:29.176
- Being alone in a
mysterious, creepy place,

00:04:29.176 --> 00:04:30.823
that would make me more afraid.

00:04:30.823 --> 00:04:32.224
- It's all about the power of the mind.

00:04:32.224 --> 00:04:33.280
If you're afraid of something,

00:04:33.280 --> 00:04:35.271
you're probably gonna force that to exist

00:04:35.271 --> 00:04:36.329
somehow in your mind.

00:04:36.329 --> 00:04:37.649
- You can believe whatever you want.

00:04:37.649 --> 00:04:38.929
I'm not gonna be the one to be like,

00:04:38.929 --> 00:04:40.777
"You're fake, you're bull, whatever."

00:04:40.777 --> 00:04:42.240
- There's a world of things

00:04:42.240 --> 00:04:43.418
humans can't perceive.

00:04:43.418 --> 00:04:45.369
Could ghosts theoretically
be one of those thing?

00:04:45.369 --> 00:04:48.112
Sure, but that's just as likely as like,

00:04:48.112 --> 00:04:50.819
cat monsters that eat squids.

00:04:53.188 --> 00:04:55.117
(quiet piano music)

00:04:55.117 --> 00:04:57.119
- It's just so sad what's
happening over there.

00:04:57.119 --> 00:04:58.713
- Oh yeah, mm-hmm.

00:05:00.455 --> 00:05:01.288
Hmmm.

00:05:01.288 --> 00:05:03.337
You don't know the half of it.

